 "notes": "GenApp's add-policy service (LGAPDB01, LINKed with the LGCMAREA COMMAREA, described by its caller LGAPOL01's record): the POLICY row is INSERTed with Db2's identity number and LASTCHANGED = CURRENT TIMESTAMP, the number read back with SET :H = IDENTITY_VAL_LOCAL() and LASTCHANGED with a SELECT, then the type's row (ENDOWMENT / HOUSE / MOTOR / COMMERCIAL), and LGAPVS01 (run in the same task) writes the VSAM copy. POLICY.LASTCHANGED and CA-LASTCHANGED (CA-REQUEST-SPECIFIC(31:26)) are clock fields, as is COMMERCIAL.REQUESTDATE (CURRENT TIMESTAMP too). A customer that does not exist is -530 ('70'), which LINKs LGSTSQ (oracle_assumptions.md X6): not here. Not here either: the endowment path MOVEs CA-E-PADDING-DATA into WS-VARY-CHAR(1:EIBCALEN - the required length), which with the 32500-byte COMMAREA its caller passes runs far past WS-VARY-CHAR's 3900 bytes -- a storage overlay (no SSRANGE) no oracle here can judge (oracle_assumptions.md X8)."
